Modifications: this is a Python adaptation, not the unchanged MAP distribution.
The binary implementation adds vectorized assembly, optional compiled tridiagonal
solves, deviation-form phase solves, composition-dependent diffusivity modes,
interstitial support, and package-specific timestep, convergence and lifecycle
controls. The ternary/two-phase and three-phase solvers are local extensions.
Source headers identify the MAP-derived binary modules; docs/LEDGERS.md records
subsequent changes and docs/BINARY_SLICE.md records the extraction provenance.
